15 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating the channel shuffle operation in convolutional neural networks. The top section depicts colored input, feature, and output channel blocks with labels, showing the process by which channels are shuffled. The middle row, labeled \215a.\216, shows a step-by-step horizontal flow where input channels labeled with colors and identifiers are rearranged through complete channel shuffle, indicating how channels and regions are reorganized. The lower section, labeled \215b.\216, includes a sample original image of a flower, blocks representing processing output, and a grayscale output image, visually connecting the channel shuffle procedure to real-world image transformation.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Panel a shows four close-up photographs of pepper plants with small white flowers surrounded by green leaves in a greenhouse setting. Panel b presents four close-up photographs of pepper plants where the flowers appear slightly wilted or are in various stages of bloom among green stems and leaves. Panel c displays four close-up photographs of pepper plants with white flowers and green leaves; one image shows a flower above a thick green stem, and another features a leaf with visible water droplets.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Flowchart diagram illustrating a four-part deep learning model: 1\) texts are embedded by BERT into vectors; 2\) multi-scale C3k2 module splits input through parallel bottleneck layers; 3\) fusion via convolution and softmax; 4\) final output tensor is produced.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Diagram comparing object detection box measurements, with part a showing GT box and PR box overlap with widths dw1, dw2 and heights dh1, dh2 marked, and part b showing distances D1, D2, D3, and D4 between the same boxes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing three nested rectangles labeled PR Box \(outer, orange\), Inner Box \(dashed orange\), and GT Box \(middle, blue\). Arrows indicate distances d1 and d2 between boxes. Center is marked as \(x sub c power P, y sub c power P\). Axes Cx and Cy are labeled.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 60 0 R /Alt (Diagram comparing bounding box alignments for object detection, with two panels labeled a and b. Both show a large orange PR Box, a smaller blue GT Box, and an Inner Box in orange dashed lines, with axes labeled C sub I x and C sub I y. Panel a displays the GT Box centrally within the PR Box, while panel b shows the GT Box positioned closer to the lower right corner of the PR Box. The centroid coordinates \(x superscript P sub c, y superscript P sub c\) are marked inside each GT Box.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 61 0 R /Alt (Panel a shows a probability density curve sharply peaking near one and asymmetric, with a cyan dashed vertical line at zero. Panel b shows a taller, narrower asymmetric curve with a black dashed vertical line at zero. Both axes range from negative five to positive five for x and zero to maximum value for y, with thick purple curve outlines.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
